  <p>
    delayed choice explores the uncertainty of perception and the temporal gap
    between an event and its recognition. The work reflects on how meaning is
    continuously reconstructed through memory rather than existing as a fixed
    reality.
  </p>

  <p>
    By combining controlled movement with subtle temporal shifts, the video
    invites the viewer to question whether what is seen is determined by the
    present moment or continuously rewritten by what follows.
  </p>

